 "title": "Saad's Definition and Example of Sales",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "Sales is about helping people rather than just taking from them. The creator explains through an example that real sales involves showing customers what they need and helping them achieve it.",
 "key_points": [
  "Sales is not taking; sales is helping.",
  "Example setup: A speaker asks Utkarsh for 100 rupees cash to buy a 500 rupees service.",
  "The speaker gives Utkarsh 500 rupees in exchange for the 100 rupees.",
  "Sales is about showing a mirror of what people actually require and helping them achieve those things.",
  "Sales is not at all about persuading someone."
 ],
 "content": "Post caption: Sales is helping! It’s a clip from @thethinkschool podcast 🙌 [Sales, real sales closing, selling] #salesandmarketing #sales #closingdeals Transcript: So sales is not taking, sales is helping. Can I show you an example? Live example? Yeah. So who has like a 100 rupees cash? Utkarsh. For that 100 rupees, I want to buy, I want you to buy my service, okay? And my service is 500 rupees. So if you pay me that 100 rupees, I will give you 500 rupees. Are you okay to do this transaction with me? Yeah. This is the 500 rupees. You want to buy this 500 from me? This is yours. Thank you. Do you see? Hey, do you see the look on his face? Do you see? Look at the smile on his face. That is sales. That was one of the finest example of how exactly sales happen. This is not at all about persuading someone, but it's more about showing them a mirror of what actually they require and how exactly you can help them to achieve those things. Text on screen: Saad explained What is Sales",
